      "content": [
       {
        "text": "Interest. Credit card interest is calculated daily on the unpaid balance and charged monthly. Paying the closing balance in full by the due date avoids purchase interest.\n\nLost or stolen cards. Customers can lock a card instantly in the app. A locked card can be unlocked; a cancelled card cannot. Staff should direct suspected fraud to the fraud procedure.",
        "source": "POL-FAQ-01#2"
       },
       {
        "text": "Wattle Bank (fictional). Use this procedure when a customer reports a stolen card, an unauthorised transaction or a scam.\n\nStep one. Recommend an immediate card block. The block is a regulated action: it is executed only after a fraud specialist approves it, or automatically by the decision service when rule R1 fires and policy allows.\n\nStep two. Never ask the customer for a full card number, PIN, or one-time passcode. Scammers impersonate bank staff to collect these.",
        "source": "POL-FRAUD-01#1"
       },
       {
        "text": "Step three. Suppress all marketing contact for the customer while the fraud flag is active. Route the case to the fraud queue with reason code FRAUD_SUSPECTED.\n\nScams. If the customer was tricked into making a payment themselves, record it as an authorised push payment scam. Recovery is attempted but not guaranteed. Do not promise a refund.",
        "source": "POL-FRAUD-01#2"
       }
